\pard\sa180\f0\fs22\cf1
\pard\sa200\sb100\f0\fs40\b\cf2 CyberFaCES SmartSearch -- Experiment Runbook\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Sequential commands to run each of the nine retrieval experiments as isolated Kubernetes Jobs in the cyberfaces-dev namespace on Purdue's Anvil cluster. Every command is copy-pasteable and assumes you are in the repository root.\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Companion to README.md, section "Running the experiments". Generated 2026-09-14 from the manifests in evaluate/k8s/.\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 Jobs are never run inside the live cyberfaces-rag Deployment. Its 4Gi memory limit OOM-kills (exit 137) when all three reranker models load at once.\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 Only one GPU slice is typically free cluster-wide. Run these ONE AT A TIME; a second Job will sit Pending with 'Insufficient nvidia.com/gpu' until the first finishes.\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 0. One-time prerequisites\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Confirm cluster access and that both secrets exist. Nothing below works without them.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil get ns cyberfaces-dev\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil get secret -n cyberfaces-dev | grep -E 'rag-secrets|hf-token'\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: cyberfaces-rag-secrets (provides ANVILGPT_API) and cyberfaces-hf-token (provides token, for the gte jobs). If the HuggingFace token is missing, create one from a free read token at huggingface.co/settings/tokens:\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 printf '%s' "hf_xxx..." > /tmp/.hf_token   # never pass a token as a CLI arg\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create secret generic cyberfaces-hf-token \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --from-file=token=/tmp/.hf_token\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 shred -u /tmp/.hf_token\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Three corpora are gitignored and must exist locally\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Course content is deliberately kept out of version control. A fresh clone will NOT have these, and five experiments cannot run without them:\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1   courses_md/             -- Experiment 2 (uploaded into the running pod)\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1   summaries/              -- Experiment 3 (the 346-file unit_N__slug.md corpus)\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1   curated_summaries_35q/  -- Experiments 4, 5 and 6 (the 239-file NNN-slug.md corpus)\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Regenerate them with extract_courses_full.py, make_module_summaries.py and generate_descriptions.py, or copy them from a machine that already has them. Verify before starting:\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 ls courses_md            | wc -l   # expect 346\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 ls summaries             | wc -l   # expect 346\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 ls curated_summaries_35q | wc -l   # expect 239\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 summaries/ and curated_summaries_35q/ are DIFFERENT corpora with different naming schemes and no overlapping files. Mixing them up silently breaks Experiments 4-6.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Reusable wait helper\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Every experiment below ends by waiting on its Job. This loop blocks until the Job reaches a terminal state, whichever it is:\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job () \{\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   until kubectl --context=anvil get job "$1" -n cyberfaces-dev \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3         -o jsonpath='\{.status.conditions[*].type\}' 2>/dev/null \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3         | grep -qE 'Complete|Failed'; do sleep 20; done\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   kubectl --context=anvil get job "$1" -n cyberfaces-dev\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 \}\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 CRITICAL: capture logs BEFORE the pod is garbage-collected. kubectl logs works on a finished pod; kubectl cp and kubectl exec do NOT. ttlSecondsAfterFinished is 86400 (24h), so anything not saved within a day is gone.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 mkdir -p evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 1. Shared ConfigMaps -- check before every run\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Jobs mount their scripts and data from ConfigMaps that live on the cluster with NO TTL, so they can be months older than your working copy. Diff before reusing; two of the five known defects came from stale copies.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil get configmap -n cyberfaces-dev\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Verify the shared answer key is the 1,035-query set (Experiments 1, 6, 7, 8, 9):\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil get configmap cyberfaces-hn-data -n cyberfaces-dev -o json \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   | python3 -c "import json,sys,base64,gzip; \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 raw=gzip.decompress(base64.b64decode(json.load(sys.stdin)['binaryData']['final_evaluation_dataset.jsonl.gz'])); \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 print('rows:', raw.count(b'\\n'))"\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 # MUST print 10428. If it prints 10024 the 996-query set was loaded by mistake.\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Regenerate cyberfaces-hn-code (Experiments 1, 3, 7, 8, 9)\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-hn-code \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=app_main.py=./app/main.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_retrievers.py=./evaluate/compare_retrievers.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=calculate_ndcg.py=./evaluate/calculate_ndcg.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_bm25_expansion.py=./evaluate/compare_bm25_expansion.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=expand_ground_truth_pool.py=./evaluate/expand_ground_truth_pool.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_hybrid_rerank.py=./evaluate/compare_hybrid_rerank.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Regenerate cyberfaces-hn-data (Experiments 1, 7, 8, 9)\b0\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 Uses `replace`, not `apply`: the payload exceeds apply's 256KiB last-applied-configuration annotation cap and apply will fail.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 gzip -9 -c ./final_evaluation_dataset_1035q.jsonl > /tmp/gt1035.jsonl.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-hn-data \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=data.jsonl=./data.jsonl \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=course_unit_map.jsonl=./course_unit_map.jsonl \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=final_evaluation_dataset.jsonl.gz=/tmp/gt1035.jsonl.gz \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil replace -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiment 1 -- BM25 vs. vector vs. vector+rerank\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 1,035-query. Runtime: about 90 seconds. Prerequisites: cyberfaces-hn-code, cyberfaces-hn-data (both above).\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/exp1-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-exp1-full\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-exp1-full --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp1_full_1035q.log\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 tail -12 evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp1_full_1035q.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: BM25 0.4159, Vector 0.5235, Vector+Jina rerank 0.4905 (NDCG@10 mean).\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiment 2 -- full document content, gte-large + jina rerank\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 996-query. TWO Jobs: the reranked arm and the semantic baseline. Requires courses_md/ locally and the HuggingFace token secret.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 2a. ConfigMap\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 gzip -9 -c ./evaluate/final_evaluation_dataset.jsonl > /tmp/gt996.jsonl.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-gte-jina-code \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_gte_vs_jina.py=./evaluate/compare_gte_vs_jina.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=calculate_ndcg.py=./evaluate/calculate_ndcg.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=ground_truth.jsonl.gz=/tmp/gt996.jsonl.gz \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 2b. Reranked arm -- needs a manual upload mid-run\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 The Job prints WAITING_FOR_UPLOAD and blocks until you push courses_md in and touch the READY flag. Runtime about 20 minutes after the upload.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 tar czf /tmp/courses_md.tar.gz -C . courses_md\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/gte-jina-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 \par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 # wait for the pod to print WAITING_FOR_UPLOAD\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 until kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-jina \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3       --tail=20 2>/dev/null | grep -q WAITING_FOR_UPLOAD; do sleep 5; done\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 \par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 POD=$(kubectl --context=anvil get pods -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-jina \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3       --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp -o jsonpath='\{.items[-1:].metadata.name\}')\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil cp /tmp/courses_md.tar.gz cyberfaces-dev/"$POD":/work/courses_md.tar.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil exec -n cyberfaces-dev "$POD" -- touch /work/READY\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 \par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-gte-jina\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-jina --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp2_gte_jina.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: Cross-enc (jina-v3) NDCG@10 0.6227, n=960.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 2c. Semantic baseline -- same upload dance, about 70 seconds\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/gte-baseline-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 until kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-baseline \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3       --tail=20 2>/dev/null | grep -q WAITING_FOR_UPLOAD; do sleep 5; done\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 POD=$(kubectl --context=anvil get pods -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-baseline \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3       --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp -o jsonpath='\{.items[-1:].metadata.name\}')\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil cp /tmp/courses_md.tar.gz cyberfaces-dev/"$POD":/work/courses_md.tar.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil exec -n cyberfaces-dev "$POD" -- touch /work/READY\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-gte-baseline\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-gte-baseline --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp2_gte_baseline.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: Semantic (gte-large) NDCG@10 0.6346, n=960. Run BOTH arms -- comparing the reranked number against the published 0.567 compares two different scoring conventions and is what made reranking look like a win.\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiment 3 -- query rewriting\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 996-query (it CANNOT be moved to the 1,035-query key: the rewrite mapping covers 996/996 queries there and only 17/1,035 here). Requires summaries/ locally. Runtime about 6 hours -- see the note below.\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 6h04m of that is the unfixed device bug at compare_rewrites_summaries.py line 108, which selects mps-or-cpu and never checks CUDA, so gte-large embeds on CPU. Fixing that line cuts the runtime dramatically.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 3a. ConfigMaps\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-exp3-code \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_query_rewrites.py=./evaluate/compare_query_rewrites.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=compare_rewrites_summaries.py=./evaluate/compare_rewrites_summaries.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 cyberfaces-exp3-data uses plain `create` after a delete -- the binary payload is too large for apply's annotation cap.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 tar czf /tmp/summaries.tar.gz summaries\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 gzip -9 -c ./evaluate/final_evaluation_dataset.jsonl > /tmp/gt996.jsonl.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil delete configmap cyberfaces-exp3-data -n cyberfaces-dev --ignore-not-found\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-exp3-data \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=summaries.tar.gz=/tmp/summaries.tar.gz \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=query_comparison.xlsx=./query_comparison.xlsx \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=gt996.jsonl.gz=/tmp/gt996.jsonl.gz \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 3b. Run\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/exp3-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-exp3-rewrites\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-exp3-rewrites --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp3_rewrites.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected, plain corpus (n=996): bm25 old 0.6799 / new 0.4441; vector old 0.8344 / new 0.5079. Summaries corpus (n=979): gte old 0.6250 / new 0.5622. Rewrites lose in every case.\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiments 4 and 5 -- text formatting and curated summaries\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 35-query hand-labeled. One Job produces both. Runtime about 4 minutes.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 4a. ConfigMaps\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-eval-flatten-ab-script \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=flatten_ab_eval.py=./flatten_ab_eval.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=gemini_generate_dataset_updateByHuman.jsonl=./gemini_generate_dataset_updateByHuman.jsonl \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 The summaries ConfigMap is built from curated_summaries_35q/ (239 files), NOT from summaries/ (346 files). They are different corpora. Building it from the wrong one silently breaks Experiments 4, 5 and 6.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-eval-flatten-ab-summaries \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=curated_summaries_35q/ \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 4b. Run\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/flatten-ab-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-eval-flatten-ab\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-eval-flatten-ab --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp45_flatten_ab.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: the log opens with '336 docs, 35 eval queries' and 'summary: 238 curated .md files, 98/336 docs fall back'. RRF current 0.861 bAcc / 0.680 MCC / 114 FP. RRF and CrossEncoder_base should match to three decimals; CrossEncoder_advance varies run to run because of LLM query rewriting.\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiment 6 -- NDCG@10 at scale\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 1,035-query. Runtime about 23 minutes. Reuses both flatten-ab ConfigMaps above, plus its own.\par
\pard\sa140\li240\f0\fs21\b\cf4 NOTE: \b0 The live cyberfaces-eval-ndcg ConfigMap also carries an extra_docs.jsonl key with no repo counterpart. Regenerating drops it. That is fine -- the Job does not set NDCG_EXTRA_DOCS_FILE, so it runs on the documented 336-document corpus either way.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 gzip -9 -c ./final_evaluation_dataset_1035q.jsonl > /tmp/gt1035.jsonl.gz\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil create configmap cyberfaces-eval-ndcg \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=ndcg_eval.py=./ndcg_eval.py \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   --from-file=final_evaluation_dataset.jsonl.gz=/tmp/gt1035.jsonl.gz \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   -n cyberfaces-dev --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl --context=anvil apply -f -\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 \par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/ndcg-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-eval-ndcg\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil logs -n cyberfaces-dev -l app=cyberfaces-eval-ndcg --tail=-1 \\\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3   > evaluate/k8s/run_logs_$(date +%F)/exp6_ndcg.log\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Expected: RRF (summary) 0.441 / 0.463, CrossEncoder_advance 0.445, with 995 scored and 40 excluded, 0 errors.\par
\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Experiment 7 -- AI query expansion for BM25\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Answer key: 1,035-query. Runtime about 25 minutes (1,035 sequential AnvilGPT calls). Prerequisites: cyberfaces-hn-code, cyberfaces-hn-data.\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil apply -f evaluate/k8s/bm25-expansion-job.yaml\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 wait_job cyberfaces-bm25-expansion\par
