\pard\sa140\sb320\f0\fs30\b\cf2 Verification and troubleshooting\b0\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Cross-checks that prove nothing has drifted\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Experiments 1, 7 and 9 each compute BM25 on the same answer key and must agree to four decimal places (0.4159 / 0.4212 NDCG@10 mean/median). If they disagree, the corpus or the answer key has changed -- that is a finding, not something to overwrite.\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 Experiment 1's vector row should match Experiment 9's to within about 0.001; small differences come from rebuilding the Chroma index, which is approximate.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Which answer key does a number belong to?\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 The 996- and 1,035-query sets share only 17 query strings and are NOT nested. BM25 scores 0.680 on the 996-query key and 0.4159 on the 1,035-query key. Never compare numbers across the two.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Pod stuck Pending\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa0\f1\fs18\cf3 kubectl --context=anvil describe pod -n cyberfaces-dev <pod> | grep -A5 Events:\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 'Insufficient nvidia.com/gpu' means every GPU node is busy. Wait, or finish the running Job first. This is normal, not a misconfiguration.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 kubectl apply fails on a ConfigMap\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 'metadata.annotations: Too long: must have at most 262144 bytes' means the payload exceeds apply's annotation cap. Use kubectl replace, or delete then plain create. Affects cyberfaces-hn-data and cyberfaces-exp3-data.\par
\pard\sa100\sb220\f0\fs24\b\cf1 Deterministic vs. nondeterministic paths\b0\par
\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf1 RRF, BM25, vector and CrossEncoder_base are deterministic and should reproduce exactly. Anything calling AnvilGPT for query rewriting or expansion -- CrossEncoder_advance, Experiment 7's expansion, Experiment 8's grading -- varies between runs. Judge those on direction and magnitude, not the third decimal.\par
